# Review ownership for the release path and the tooling that drives it.
#
# GitHub consults this file ONLY when it evaluates a pull request's reviews, and ONLY from the
# branch that pull request TARGETS -- never from the default branch. On its own it blocks
# nothing: what gives it force is whichever org ruleset applies to THIS branch. The file exists
# on each of the three branches separately and is kept identical across them.
#
# The operator's branch policy requires an admin for any pull request into `dev` or `test`
# that touches CI or scripts, and requires an admin to merge into `prod` at all. This file is
# the whole implementation of the first half; a path absent from this list is a path any
# developer may change and merge alone. It is deliberately BROAD -- all of `/scripts/`.
#
# There are three branches and only three: `dev`, `test`, `prod`.

